# Force LF line endings for Rust sources — rustc 1.91+ rejects bare CR in
# source files (CRCRLF on Windows checkouts otherwise breaks `cargo check`
# with "carriage return must be followed by newline").
rust/**/*.rs    text eol=lf
rust/**/*.toml  text eol=lf
rust/Cargo.toml text eol=lf
rust/Cargo.lock text eol=lf

# Rust: rustc 1.91+ rejects bare CR in source. Force LF on checkout/checkin.

# .NET sources and project files: force LF. Some .cs files carried malformed
# double-CR (\r\r\n) endings (which inflate line counts 2x and cause diff noise);
# normalize going forward. Bulk `git add --renormalize` of existing files is a
# separate task. LF matches the cross-platform (Windows + macOS) build.
*.cs      text eol=lf
*.csproj  text eol=lf
*.props   text eol=lf
*.targets text eol=lf
*.slnx    text eol=lf
